],[70,1],[90,3],[70,2],[90,23],[70,1],[90,1],[70,3],[90,1],[70,6],[90,22],[70,14],[90,6],[70,1],[90,23],[70,2],[90,32],[70,1]],"losingConfidence":0}},{"accession":"Q9UBC3-3","name":"DNMT3B3","synonyms":[],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Inactive isoform that lacks (cytosine-5)-methyltransferase activity and acts as an accessory factor for de novo DNA methylation (PubMed:27121154, PubMed:32968275). Forms a heterotetramer complex with catalytic isoforms from DNMT3A or DNMT3B, and acts as a scaffold to bridge the heterotetramer complex to nucleosomes and orient the catalytic subunit toward the accessible linker DNA (PubMed:32968275). The heterotetramer complex specifically methylates long DNA linker regions between two nucleosomes (PubMed:41742418). In contrast, short DNA linker regions, which are enriched at promoter regions, promote di-nucleosome bridging, blocking access to linker DNA, preventing methylation (PubMed:41742418). Stimulates the activity of DNMT3A (isoforms DNMT3A1 or DNMT3A2) and DNMT3B (isoforms DNMT3B1 or DNMT3B2), with a preference for DNMT3B-mediated DNA methylation (By similarity)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Heterotetramer composed of two regulatory DNMT3B3 subunits and a catalytic homodimer (either isoforms DNMT3A1 or DNMT3A2 of DNMT3A or isoforms DNMT3B1 or DNMT3B2 of DNMT3B)"}],"length":770,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000348286.6"],"refseq":["NM_175849.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_787045.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,355],[356,376,369],[725,808,46]],"edits":[{"start":356,"end":375,"original":"VVNKSKVRRAGSRKLESRKY","replacement":"","added":0},{"start":745,"end":807,"original":"PVIASKNDKLELQDCLEYNRIAKLKKVQTITTKSNSIKQG","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":83,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":63,"foldedMissing":63,"features":[[28,63,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q9UBC3-3-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q9UBC3-3-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":67.9,"plddt":[[0,214],[50,1]